#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_riccati_solve

#% text
# `discrete_riccati_solve([a, b], [q, r])` gives the stabilizing solution x of the discrete algebraic Riccati equation `a^H . x . a - x - a^H . x . b . (r + b^H . x . b)^-1 . b^H . x . a + q == 0`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The solution comes from the structure-preserving doubling iteration; the result is a machine-number matrix.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
discrete_riccati_solve([[[0, 2], [1, 0]], [[0], [1]]], [[[1, 0], [0, 4/9]], [[1]]])
#% output
#= [[1.8888888888888886, 0.0], [0.0, 8.0]]

#% cell
discrete_riccati_solve([[[-1, 0.5], [-0.5, -2]], [[1], [0.5]]], [[[1, 0], [0, 2]], [[1]]])
#% output
#= [[1.9250566939144111, 2.610775872464342], [2.610775872464342, 31.23034923871982]]

